TITLE: T45-O Native Developmental Integration Candidate
DATE: 2026-10-20
STATUS: UNQUALIFIED DRAFT
TRACK: DG-1 / Optimizer T45-O
QUESTION
Can local learned cell prediction be called through maintained Yggdrasil source,
retain differentiated parameters, and survive bounded lesion/restore checks?

IMPLEMENTATION
- Candidate-only reusable Python module yggdrasil/cells.py.
- scripts/native_cells.py: offline JSONL entrypoint; 1 MiB input budget.
- Each cell receives only its own and immediate ring-neighbor previous states,
  with its own subsequent outcome; no role labels or global controller.
- Bound eight cells and seven weights each; state snapshot has explicit schema.
- Lesion and neighbor-copy are available for falsification; neighbor-copy is
  redundancy and NOT evidence of true developmental regeneration.

LIMITS
This is an intentionally conventional source-free learning component.
An optimal count table was superior in T45-N; the new module does NOT establish
novel general cognition, full native Yggdrasil runtime deployment, independently
sealed source use, total-resource superiority or scientific acceptance.

AUTHORITY
No FORGE research dispatch, source birth, production activation or promotion.
FORGE-native FSA must independently qualify any future scientific claim.
No CKB-plane research execution or acceptance dependency.
